Copy this file to sentry-dsn.local (gitignored) and put the hosted-Sentry
fallback DSN in it, on one line, for a rollback build.

    https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>

Never commit the real file. Three things keep it out of the public repository
and they are all deliberate: `.gitignore` excludes `*.local`, the publish script
excludes the same pattern from the snapshot, and its secrets guard matches a DSN
by shape as a backstop.

Packaging refuses to continue if crashbox-dsn.local is also populated, so a
release has exactly one destination and never dual-sends. Without either file
the packaged app carries an empty reporting address, and crash reporting cannot
be switched on however the toggle is set.
